{"judgments": [
  {
    "clause_id": "c001",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The paragraph turns on several open-textured terms — \"the Business\" defined only as \"Spanish language and bilingual print and media business\", capital \"in an amount that DMSA deems appropriate\", and \"all expenditures must be done with the concurrence of DMSA\" — each of which two parties could plausibly read differently, and it says nothing about what LSB contributes beyond \"not ... any cash\", leaving the pre-existing Dialogo publication's status unstated.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "Its mandatory annual tax distribution and pro-rata profit distribution sit awkwardly against Paragraph 4's waterfall, which subordinates the tax distribution to full repayment of DMSA's unilaterally-sized initial capital and makes any remainder discretionary with the Board; it also interacts uneasily with Paragraph 3's reference to \"Dialogo\" as an existing staffed business rather than the newly-formed LLC.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.58,
    "prob_cat2": 0.54
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c002",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The one-sided structure — DMSA free to keep and originate business while LSB is bound by \"diligent efforts\" and a non-compete reaching anything \"to the extent it relates to the Business\" — plus the merely precatory \"intends to use diligent efforts\", gives a court plainly nameable vague terms and a contra proferentem/one-sidedness point.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "The freedom it gives DMSA and its principals to compete pulls against Paragraph 1's statement that the parties form the LLC \"for the purpose of jointly developing\" the Business and against the opening promise here to \"jointly pursue the Business\"; it also switches to \"the Company\", a term defined nowhere in Paragraph 1.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.55,
    "prob_cat2": 0.42
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c003",
    "reasoning_cat1": "A single undefined sentence: \"the staffs of DMSA and Dialogo\" uses \"Dialogo\" — the name Paragraph 1 gives to the LLC itself — so it either refers circularly to the new LLC or, more likely, to LSB's pre-existing Dialogo newspaper, and \"initially rely on\" fixes neither duration nor payment.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "Read against Paragraph 1, which names the LLC \"Dialogo\" and says LSB contributes no cash and nothing else, this sentence is the only hint that an existing Dialogo business and its staff come into the venture, which is precisely the kind of unreconciled gap a court must construe.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.62,
    "prob_cat2": 0.58
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c004",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The text is materially garbled and at least one sentence trails off unfinished (\"it is the Domd of Dibemes nee wilt barron, + but thet may' our in thi Sunure Hf eppreved by\"), and the waterfall's first tier — reimbursement of unspecified \"out of pocket costs\" — and the \"approved budget\" are undefined.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It conflicts with Paragraph 1: there the board \"shall distribute each year at least enough cash\" for owners' taxes and all distributed profits go pro rata, whereas here tax money ranks only third behind repayment of DMSA's self-determined initial capital and the residue is discretionary.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.55,
    "prob_cat2": 0.52
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c005",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The definition of \"Proprietary Information\" is a long enumerated list closing with the broad, undelimited \"client provided information, documents and data\", raising an ejusdem generis/scope question, and the provision has no time limit or carve-out for information already known to a party.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It coexists with Paragraph 2, which lets DMSA and its principals retain and originate advertising contracts and clients for their own benefit — potentially using the very client lists this paragraph makes confidential to the LLC — a tension worth construing, though the paragraphs can arguably be harmonised.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.44,
    "prob_cat2": 0.33
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c006",
    "reasoning_cat1": "It is an agreement to execute further documents on unstated \"standard terms and conditions\", with a duplicated verb and an incomplete list, so whether it binds the parties to anything definite is genuinely arguable.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "Its contemplation of an articles of organization and an operating agreement yet to be negotiated bears on whether the whole instrument (including Paragraph 1's promise that \"the owners will sign an agreement\" on transfers) is a binding contract or a preliminary memorandum — a whole-instrument question a court would have to answer.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.48,
    "prob_cat2": 0.40
  }
]}

